  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Some photos from the Apollo Moon landings of 1969 show shadows that cross each other, which some take as a sign of more than one light source, when the Sun should be the only one. The podcaster Joe Rogan raises it in conversation with Michels, saying people like to try to dismiss these intersecting shadows. If the point held, it would mean the pictures were not lit by sunlight alone."
